<title>FRANCE: French CFDT union says shipyard stoppages Thursday.</title>
<headline>French CFDT union says shipyard stoppages Thursday.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-09-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>France's Socialist CFDT union said on Tuesday further short strikes had been called for Thursday at naval shipyards in a follow-up to stoppages on September 10.</p>
<p>&quot;After the nationwide action of September 10, staff at the shipyards will be back in action after a call from their union federations,&quot; a CFDT statement said.</p>
<p>Stoppages of one to two hours have been called for at naval yards in Brest, Lorient, Cherbourg, Indret, Ruelle and Toulon.</p>
<p>The strikes are part of protests against cuts in the defence sector and plans that could mean employment location moves for staff under a labour mobility programme.</p>
</text>
